<title>TUNISIA: Tunisian insurance firm Maghrebia '96 profits up.</title>
<headline>Tunisian insurance firm Maghrebia '96 profits up.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisian insurance firm Maghrebia Assurances made a 1.395 million dinars net profits in 1996, up from 1.152 million dinars in 1995, results showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said it would distribute a five percent statutary dividend and a three percent superdividend from August 1.</p>
<p>The firm, which was established in 1974 and has a capital of three million dinars, includes among its shareholders Italy's Assicurazione d'Italia, Assitalia, Groupe INA, and Spain's MAPFRE International S.A. Lebanon's Societe Nationale d'Assurance has also a stake in the capital.</p>
<p>Maghrebia Assurances says it was the fourth largest insurance firm in Tunisia and the first in life insurance branch. ($=1.0981 dinar)</p>
<p>- Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
